2026-08-02: Characterized immutable scoring, legal task-label joins, split/date/channel/entity distributions, warm/cold discrepancy, coverage axes, and panel aggregation throughput. Added PLAN.md and eval_profile.md at repository root because kapso_evaluation is immutable.
RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.entrypoints, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas, core.dependencies
2026-08-02: Implemented task-label-only weekly article×channel panels, four price/count lags, regime and hierarchy/cross-channel states, weighted changed-state and transition heads, forward-OOF calibration, customer-aware OOF row residual adjustment, and a 26-week recency-weighted cold launch head using static metadata plus 32D word/character TF-IDF SVD. Debug evaluation passed at validation R² 0.9315045780; first full run archived as run_0001 at R² 0.9367766376.
2026-08-02: Forward-only historical launch audit found raw launch MSE 1.4317e-4, hierarchy cascade MSE 2.5972e-4, and hierarchy-residual launch MSE 1.2418e-4; adopted the residual formulation because both mean and worst-fold MSE improved without consulting official validation labels.
2026-08-02: The hierarchy-residual full run archived as run_0005 at R² 0.9465138394. Added temporally shifted product/channel/category historical launch-price priors only after a three-fold train-only audit improved every fold and reduced mean launch MSE from 1.2543e-4 to 1.1177e-4.
2026-08-02: The launch-prior full run archived as run_0008 at R² 0.9556059162. Widened the OOF row residual with 35-day and channel-specific customer affinity/activity, affinity dispersion, and channel mix while preserving origin-time censoring.
2026-08-02: Customer-widened run_0011 scored R² 0.9555249120, within 0.000081 of run_0008. A train-only launch audit found positive shift coefficients toward the launch-history cascade in all three folds (0.094, 0.301, 0.313); added a conservative 0.20 cold calibration while retaining one 800-tree launch head.
2026-08-02: Cold-calibrated run_0014 scored R² 0.9557854498. Cached panel OOF forecasts yielded independently similar transition shrinkage (Model A 0.534, Model B 0.499); adopted the learned blend only when every paired forward fold and the aggregate improve over frozen state.
2026-08-02: Transition-blend run_0016 was TESTED-REJECTED at R² 0.9541274153 after its live OOF audit rejected both chain blends for paired-fold deterioration and fell back to state-only forecasts. Restored the solution's aggregate-mean/worst-fold transition gate; this decision follows the train-only OOF rejection rather than the official validation delta.
2026-08-02: Restored-gate run_0017 scored R² 0.9559768433. Added metadata-only origin-day article/channel volume, channel share, first-seen age, and cumulative activity from the projected transaction inputs; no database price field is selected.
2026-08-02: Snapshot-activity run_0020 scored R² 0.9546766093. Train-only OOF retained snapshot features for the panel decoder (calibrated panel MSE 3.3157e-5 versus 3.3296e-5) but rejected them for cold launch (mean 1.1223e-4 versus 1.0901e-4 and worse worst-fold MSE), so the final cold head excludes them.
